---
import LearningFigure from './LearningFigure.astro';

interface Props {
  view: 'pain' | 'body-care' | 'giving';
}

const { view } = Astro.props;
---

{
  view === 'pain' ? (
    <LearningFigure id="participant-pain" title="Wer hat Schmerzen – was tut weh?" sourceClass="simulated">
      <div slot="visual" class="role-grid" aria-hidden="true">
        <section class="role-card">
          <span class="role-question">Wem?</span>
          <div class="person-icon">●</div>
          <strong class="role-dative">mir</strong>
          <small>Person · Dativ</small>
        </section>
        <div class="role-arrow"><span>→</span><b>tut</b><small>Singular</small></div>
        <section class="role-card">
          <span class="role-question">Was?</span>
          <div class="body-icon">◉</div>
          <strong>der Kopf</strong>
          <small>Subjekt · Singular</small>
        </section>
        <div class="role-sentence"><b>Mir</b> <strong>tut</strong> der Kopf weh.</div>

        <section class="role-card">
          <span class="role-question">Wem?</span>
          <div class="person-icon">●</div>
          <strong class="role-dative">mir</strong>
          <small>Person · Dativ</small>
        </section>
        <div class="role-arrow"><span>→</span><b>tun</b><small>Plural</small></div>
        <section class="role-card">
          <span class="role-question">Was?</span>
          <div class="body-icon">◉ ◉</div>
          <strong>die Augen</strong>
          <small>Subjekt · Plural</small>
        </section>
        <div class="role-sentence"><b>Mir</b> <strong>tun</strong> die Augen weh.</div>
      </div>
      <p slot="caption" lang="de">
        Die Person steht im <strong>Dativ</strong>. Die Körperteile sind das Subjekt:
        ein Teil bestimmt <strong>tut</strong>, mehrere bestimmen <strong>tun</strong>.
      </p>
      <div slot="description">
        <p class="lang-en">Two rows separate the person in pain from the body part. In both rows the person is mir, marked as dative. In the first row der Kopf is a singular subject and therefore selects tut. In the second, die Augen is a plural subject and selects tun.</p>
        <p class="lang-ru">Две строки отделяют человека от части тела. В обеих строках человек выражен формой mir в Dativ. В первой строке der Kopf — подлежащее в единственном числе, поэтому глагол имеет форму tut. Во второй die Augen — подлежащее во множественном числе, поэтому форма глагола — tun.</p>
        <p class="lang-uk">Два рядки відокремлюють людину від частини тіла. В обох рядках людина виражена формою mir у Dativ. У першому рядку der Kopf — підмет в однині, тому дієслово має форму tut. У другому die Augen — підмет у множині, тому форма дієслова — tun.</p>
      </div>
    </LearningFigure>
  ) : view === 'body-care' ? (
    <LearningFigure id="participant-body-care" title="mich oder mir?" sourceClass="simulated">
      <div slot="visual" class="care-grid" aria-hidden="true">
        <section class="care-card">
          <span class="role-question">ohne Objekt</span>
          <div class="care-scene"><span>Person</span><b>↺</b></div>
          <p>Ich wasche <strong class="role-accusative">mich</strong>.</p>
          <small><b>mich</b> · Akkusativobjekt</small>
        </section>
        <section class="care-card">
          <span class="role-question">mit Körperteil</span>
          <div class="care-scene"><span>Person</span><b>→</b><span>Hände</span></div>
          <p>Ich wasche <strong class="role-dative">mir</strong> <strong class="role-accusative">die Hände</strong>.</p>
          <small><b>mir</b> · betroffene Person · Dativ</small>
          <small><b>die Hände</b> · Objekt · Akkusativ</small>
        </section>
      </div>
      <p slot="caption" lang="de">
        Ohne eigenes Objekt ist <strong>mich</strong> das Objekt. Mit einem Körperteil
        bezeichnet <strong>mir</strong> die betroffene Person; <strong>die Hände</strong>
        sind das Akkusativobjekt.
      </p>
      <div slot="description">
        <p class="lang-en">The left card has only one participant after the verb: mich is the accusative object in Ich wasche mich. The right card adds the body part as a separate object. Mir marks the affected owner in the dative, while die Hände is the accusative object. The ordinary German sentence uses the article die, not a possessive.</p>
        <p class="lang-ru">В левой карточке после глагола только один участник: mich — дополнение в Akkusativ в Ich wasche mich. В правой карточке часть тела становится отдельным дополнением. Mir обозначает затронутого владельца в Dativ, а die Hände — дополнение в Akkusativ. В обычной немецкой фразе используется артикль die, а не притяжательное местоимение.</p>
        <p class="lang-uk">У лівій картці після дієслова лише один учасник: mich — додаток в Akkusativ у Ich wasche mich. У правій картці частина тіла стає окремим додатком. Mir позначає людину-власника у Dativ, а die Hände — додаток в Akkusativ. У звичайній німецькій фразі вживається артикль die, а не присвійний займенник.</p>
      </div>
    </LearningFigure>
  ) : (
    <LearningFigure id="participant-giving" title="Wer gibt wem was?" sourceClass="simulated">
      <div slot="visual" class="giving-grid" aria-hidden="true">
        <section class="role-card giving-person">
          <span class="role-question">Wer?</span>
          <svg class="avatar-icon" viewBox="0 0 48 48" role="presentation">
            <circle cx="24" cy="16" r="8"></circle>
            <path d="M9 41c1.4-9 6.4-13.5 15-13.5S37.6 32 39 41"></path>
          </svg>
          <strong>Nina</strong>
          <small>Geberin · Nominativ</small>
        </section>
        <div class="transfer">
          <b class="transfer-verb">gibt</b>
          <div class="transfer-path">
            <svg class="flow-arrow" viewBox="0 0 240 48" role="presentation">
              <path d="M4 24h226"></path>
              <path d="m215 9 15 15-15 15"></path>
            </svg>
            <div class="object-token">
              <span class="role-question">Was?</span>
              <svg class="key-icon" viewBox="0 0 64 32" role="presentation">
                <circle cx="14" cy="16" r="9"></circle>
                <path d="M23 16h32M44 16v8M52 16v5"></path>
              </svg>
              <strong class="role-accusative">den Schlüssel</strong>
              <small>Sache · Akkusativ</small>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <section class="role-card giving-person">
          <span class="role-question">Wem?</span>
          <svg class="avatar-icon" viewBox="0 0 48 48" role="presentation">
            <circle cx="24" cy="16" r="8"></circle>
            <path d="M9 41c1.4-9 6.4-13.5 15-13.5S37.6 32 39 41"></path>
          </svg>
          <strong class="role-dative">dem Nachbarn</strong>
          <small>Empfänger · Dativ</small>
        </section>
      </div>
      <p slot="caption" lang="de">
        Nina gibt dem Nachbarn den Schlüssel: Sie handelt, er empfängt, und der Schlüssel
        wechselt den Besitzer.
      </p>
      <div slot="description">
        <p class="lang-en">A continuous arrow runs from Nina, the giver and nominative subject, to dem Nachbarn, the recipient in the dative. One key is attached to the transfer path and labelled den Schlüssel, the thing transferred and accusative object. The sentence is Nina gibt dem Nachbarn den Schlüssel.</p>
        <p class="lang-ru">Непрерывная стрелка ведёт от Нины — того, кто даёт, и подлежащего в Nominativ — к dem Nachbarn, получателю в Dativ. На линии передачи показан один ключ с подписью den Schlüssel: это передаваемая вещь и дополнение в Akkusativ. Полное предложение: Nina gibt dem Nachbarn den Schlüssel.</p>
        <p class="lang-uk">Безперервна стрілка веде від Ніни — тієї, хто дає, і підмета в Nominativ — до dem Nachbarn, одержувача в Dativ. На лінії передачі показано один ключ із підписом den Schlüssel: це передана річ і додаток в Akkusativ. Повне речення: Nina gibt dem Nachbarn den Schlüssel.</p>
      </div>
    </LearningFigure>
  )
}

<style>
  .role-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(7rem, 1fr) 5rem minmax(9rem, 1.2fr) minmax(13rem, 1.5fr);
    align-items: center;
    gap: .75rem;
    padding: 1.25rem;
  }
  .role-card, .care-card {
    min-width: 0;
    border: 1px solid #d6d3d1;
    border-radius: .8rem;
    background: rgb(255 255 255 / .94);
    padding: .9rem;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .role-card strong { display: block; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .role-card small, .care-card small { display: block; margin-top: .25rem; color: #57534e; }
  .role-question { display: block; margin-bottom: .45rem; color: #57534e; font-size: .7rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .person-icon, .body-icon { margin: .15rem auto .4rem; color: #44403c; font-size: 2rem; line-height: 1; }
  .outlined { font-size: 2.3rem; }
  .role-dative { color: #075985; }
  .role-accusative { color: #9a3412; }
  .role-arrow { text-align: center; }
  .role-arrow span { display: block; color: #78716c; font-size: 2rem; }
  .role-arrow b, .role-arrow small { display: block; }
  .role-sentence { border-left: 4px solid #78716c; padding: .7rem .8rem; background: rgb(255 255 255 / .72); }
  .role-sentence b { color: #075985; }
  .role-sentence strong { color: #9a3412; }
  .care-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; padding: 1.25rem; }
  .care-card p { margin: .8rem 0 .35rem; font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .care-scene { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: .65rem; min-height: 4rem; }
  .care-scene span { border: 2px solid #78716c; border-radius: 999px; padding: .45rem .7rem; font-weight: 700; }
  .care-scene b { font-size: 1.6rem; }
  .giving-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(9rem, 1fr) minmax(15rem, 1.45fr) minmax(11rem, 1.1fr);
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 1.25rem;
  }
  .giving-person { position: relative; z-index: 1; }
  .avatar-icon {
    display: block;
    width: 3rem;
    height: 3rem;
    margin: .1rem auto .4rem;
    color: #44403c;
    fill: none;
    stroke: currentColor;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
    stroke-width: 2.5;
  }
  .transfer { min-width: 0; text-align: center; }
  .transfer-verb {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: .35rem;
    padding: .2rem .6rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: #e7e5e4;
    color: #292524;
    font-size: .85rem;
  }
  .transfer-path {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    min-height: 8.5rem;
    place-items: center;
  }
  .flow-arrow {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 50% 0 auto;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    color: #78716c;
    fill: none;
    stroke: currentColor;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
    stroke-width: 3;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
  }
  .object-token {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    min-width: 10rem;
    border: 1px solid #fdba74;
    border-radius: .75rem;
    background: #fff7ed;
    padding: .55rem .8rem .65rem;
    box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgb(41 37 36 / .08);
  }
  .object-token .role-question { margin-bottom: .2rem; color: #9a3412; }
  .object-token strong, .object-token small { display: block; }
  .object-token small { margin-top: .2rem; color: #57534e; }
  .key-icon {
    display: block;
    width: 3.25rem;
    height: auto;
    margin: 0 auto .2rem;
    color: #b45309;
    fill: none;
    stroke: currentColor;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
    stroke-width: 3;
  }
  :global([data-theme='dark']) .role-card,
  :global([data-theme='dark']) .care-card { border-color: #57534e; background: rgb(41 37 36 / .94); }
  :global([data-theme='dark']) .role-card small,
  :global([data-theme='dark']) .care-card small,
  :global([data-theme='dark']) .role-question { color: #d6d3d1; }
  :global([data-theme='dark']) .role-dative { color: #7dd3fc; }
  :global([data-theme='dark']) .role-accusative { color: #fdba74; }
  :global([data-theme='dark']) .role-sentence { background: rgb(41 37 36 / .75); }
  :global([data-theme='dark']) .avatar-icon { color: #d6d3d1; }
  :global([data-theme='dark']) .transfer-verb { background: #292524; color: #e7e5e4; }
  :global([data-theme='dark']) .object-token {
    border-color: #9a3412;
    background: #29201b;
    box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgb(0 0 0 / .25);
  }
  :global([data-theme='dark']) .object-token .role-question { color: #fdba74; }
  :global([data-theme='dark']) .object-token small { color: #d6d3d1; }
  :global([data-theme='dark']) .key-icon { color: #fb923c; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .role-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 3rem minmax(0, 1fr); padding: .8rem; gap: .45rem; }
    .role-sentence { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
    .care-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; padding: .8rem; }
  }
  /* The giving grid stacks earlier than the other two, because its three
     minimum tracks (9 + 15 + 11rem) plus gaps and padding need 632px of
     content — more than the article has until the viewport reaches 664px.
     Stacking only at 640px left 641–663px clipping the recipient column
     against LearningFigure's hidden overflow, which is the one relation the
     figure exists to show. 767px keeps headroom without moving the other
     figures' breakpoint. */
  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .giving-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); padding: .8rem; gap: .4rem; }
    .transfer-path { min-height: 10rem; }
    .flow-arrow {
      inset: 50% auto auto 50%;
      width: 10rem;
      transform: translate(-50%, -50%) rotate(90deg);
    }
    .object-token { min-width: min(12rem, calc(100% - 2.5rem)); }
  }
</style>
